6. Le Cam Deficiency Bound on \eta_{\mathrm{info}}

Let \mathcal{E}_{VR}=\{P_\theta^{V,R}:\theta\in\Theta\} be the full experiment emitting (V,R), and \mathcal{E}_{V(\lambda)}=\{P_\theta^{V(\lambda)}:\theta\in\Theta\} the leaked experiment. The one-sided Le Cam deficiency is

\delta\big(\mathcal{E}_{V(\lambda)},\mathcal{E}_{VR}\big)
=
\inf_{M}\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}
\big\|MP_\theta^{V(\lambda)}-P_\theta^{V,R}\big\|_{\mathrm{TV}},

where M ranges over Markov kernels reconstructing (V,R) from V(\lambda).

Proposition 4 (Deficiency bound). For a capability functional generated by a bounded loss \ell\in[0,M_\ell], and an oracle student restricted to the reachable class,

G^{\mathrm{oracle}}_{\mathcal{S}}(V,R)-G^{\mathrm{oracle}}_{\mathcal{S}}\big(V(\lambda)\big)
\le
M_\ell\,\delta\big(\mathcal{E}_{V(\lambda)},\mathcal{E}_{VR}\big).

Consequently,

\boxed{\;\eta_{\mathrm{info}}(\lambda)
\le
\alpha\nu\,
\frac{M_\ell\,\delta\big(\mathcal{E}_{V(\lambda)},\mathcal{E}_{VR}\big)}
{G^{\mathrm{oracle}}_{\mathcal{S}}(V,R)-G_{\mathcal{S}}(\varnothing)}.\;}

For an erasure channel in which V(\lambda) reveals R with probability \lambda and erases to the marginal with probability 1-\lambda, the optimal kernel imputes the prior, giving

\delta\big(\mathcal{E}_{V(\lambda)},\mathcal{E}_{VR}\big)=(1-\lambda)\,\delta_0,

and by Pinsker’s inequality \delta_0\le\sqrt{\tfrac12 I(R;\Theta\mid V)}. The bound is O(\delta): it is a loose upper bound, not a tight characterization, and the proxy \lambda(V)=1-G_{\mathrm{distill}}(V(\lambda))/G_{\mathrm{distill}}(R) is a first-order variational estimator of 1-\delta(\lambda)/\delta_0.

