7. Causal Identification of the Optimization Component

The format-matched nulls R_{\mathrm{neutral}} (filler) and R_{\mathrm{weak}} (imperfect teacher) both alter the joint distribution P(X,V,R), either by injecting attention-diluting noise or by inducing gradient conflict. A provably neutral control requires a null that preserves the conditional distribution of R given (X,V) while carrying zero additional information about \Theta:

I(R_{\mathrm{null}};\Theta\mid X,V)=0,
\qquad
P(R_{\mathrm{null}}\mid X,V)=P(R\mid X,V).

Construct R_{\mathrm{null}}\sim P(R\mid X,V) from an auxiliary generator trained solely on observed (X,V,R) triples, without access to \Theta or unseen test queries. Then \Theta\to(X,V)\to R_{\mathrm{null}} is a Markov chain, so the data processing inequality gives I(R_{\mathrm{null}};\Theta\mid X,V)=0 identically.

Proposition 5 (Telescoping decomposition with zero interaction). Define

\eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}
=
\frac{G(V+R_{\mathrm{null}})-G(V)}{G(V,R)-G(\varnothing)},
\qquad
\eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}}
=
\frac{G(V,R)-G(V+R_{\mathrm{null}})}{G(V,R)-G(\varnothing)}.

Then

\eta=\eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}}+\eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}},
\qquad
\eta_{\mathrm{int}}\equiv 0,

because (V)\subset(V,R_{\mathrm{null}})\subset(V,R) is an exact intermediate rung on the filtration.

Interpretation. \eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}>0 isolates pure scaffolding gain; \eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}<0 isolates narrative–discriminative interference; \eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}} isolates the epistemic value of true latent trace content beyond plausible post-hoc rationalization. The construction is a proposed identification strategy, not a validated method: training the auxiliary generator for P(R\mid X,V) without leakage of \Theta remains an open implementation problem.

