8. Architecture and Algorithms

8.1 Estimation of \alpha, \nu, and \eta_{\mathrm{info}}

Algorithm 1: Reachability diagnostic.

1. Initialize the student, fix \mathcal{P} from architecture and initialization.
2. At each training step t, compute a sketched basis \widehat{\mathcal{K}}^{V}_t of recent V-supervised gradients via online PCA or sketched SVD with rank cutoff and forgetting factor.
3. Compute g_R on a matched batch.
4. \widehat{\alpha}_t=\|\Pi_{\mathcal{P}}g_R\|/\|g_R\|; \widehat{\nu}_t=\|(I-\Pi_{\widehat{\mathcal{K}}^{V}_t})\Pi_{\mathcal{P}}g_R\|/\|\Pi_{\mathcal{P}}g_R\|.
5. Report time-averaged \widehat{\alpha},\widehat{\nu} with bootstrap confidence intervals, and a null control on pure-noise “traces.”

8.2 2\times 2 Factorial for Supervision \times Objective

 Standard objective Joint teacher–student objective
V only G(V;\mathrm{std}) G(V;\mathrm{joint})
V+R G(V,R;\mathrm{std}) G(V,R;\mathrm{joint})

The supervision main effect is

\Delta_{\mathrm{sup}}=\tfrac12\big[G(V,R;\mathrm{std})-G(V;\mathrm{std})+G(V,R;\mathrm{joint})-G(V;\mathrm{joint})\big],

and the interaction is

\Delta_{\mathrm{int}}=\big[G(V,R;\mathrm{joint})-G(V;\mathrm{joint})\big]-\big[G(V,R;\mathrm{std})-G(V;\mathrm{std})\big].

\Delta_{\mathrm{sup}} estimates the residual attributable to R averaged over objectives; \Delta_{\mathrm{int}} estimates the optimization-course contribution. The joint-objective condition is pre-registered in both an R-conditioned and a V-derived variant, so that the factorial separates supervision from privileged-information conditioning.

8.3 Causal Null Construction

Algorithm 2: Posterior-predictive null.

1. Train an auxiliary generator \widehat{P}(R\mid X,V) on observed triples, with a strict information barrier to \Theta and held-out queries.
2. Sample R_{\mathrm{null}}\sim\widehat{P}(\cdot\mid X,V) for each training example.
3. Train the student on (V,R_{\mathrm{null}}) under the standard objective.
4. Compute \eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}} and \eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}} from Proposition 5.
5. Audit I(R_{\mathrm{null}};\Theta\mid X,V) empirically via a held-out mutual-information estimator; a positive estimate invalidates the null.

8.4 Budget Stratification

The three-way stratum \times condition \times K contrast is reported across at least four sampling budgets K, with B^* estimated from Proposition 3 and TAS@K computed before training to pre-register the expected sign of d\eta/dB. A pure-reasoning stratum is evaluated separately from the action-observable agentic stratum, because the reachability factor \alpha and the tail mass \pi_{\mathrm{tail}} need not behave identically across the two.

