Appendix G: Posterior-Predictive Null Construction

G.1 Definition

Let R_{\mathrm{null}}\sim P(R\mid X,V) be drawn from an auxiliary generator \widehat{P}(R\mid X,V) trained only on observed triples, with no access to \Theta and no access to held-out queries. The data-processing inequality for the Markov chain \Theta\to(X,V)\to R_{\mathrm{null}} gives

I(R_{\mathrm{null}};\Theta\mid X,V)=0.

G.2 Telescoping Decomposition

Define

\eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}
=
\frac{G(V+R_{\mathrm{null}})-G(V)}{G(V,R)-G(\varnothing)},
\qquad
\eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}}
=
\frac{G(V,R)-G(V+R_{\mathrm{null}})}{G(V,R)-G(\varnothing)}.

Adding the two expressions,

\eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}+\eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}}
=
\frac{G(V,R)-G(V)}{G(V,R)-G(\varnothing)}
=
\eta,

so the interaction residual is identically zero:

\eta_{\mathrm{int}}
=
\eta-\eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}}-\eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}
\equiv 0.

The decomposition is exact because (V)\subset(V,R_{\mathrm{null}})\subset(V,R) is a filtration and the three capability differences telescope.

G.3 Interpretation

· \eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}>0: uninformative but format-matched rationales improve capability through scaffolding, gradient variance reduction, or step-level credit assignment.
· \eta_{\mathrm{opt}}^{\mathrm{causal}}<0: narrative–discriminative interference dominates, as in the synthetic-rationale evidence where rationale-based SFT consistently hurts prediction relative to label-only fine-tuning across 504 configurations.
· \eta_{\mathrm{info}}^{\mathrm{causal}}: epistemic value of the true trace beyond what a plausible post-hoc rationalization already provides.

G.4 Audit

The construction is valid only if the auxiliary generator does not leak \Theta. Estimate I(R_{\mathrm{null}};\Theta\mid X,V) empirically on a held-out set with a mutual-information estimator (e.g., a classifier distinguishing (R_{\mathrm{null}},X,V) pairs drawn with and without \Theta-dependent conditioning). A positive estimate invalidates the null and the decomposition. This audit is a necessary condition, not a sufficient one: zero estimated mutual information on a finite sample is consistent with a small positive value.

G.5 Implementation Barrier

Training \widehat{P}(R\mid X,V) without leakage is the main open problem. Candidate procedures include backward rationalization from (X,V) alone, prompt-conditioned generation with the teacher’s trace removed from the conditioning context, and adversarial filtering of generations that encode \Theta-specific content. None of these is established as sufficient; the construction is therefore a proposed identification strategy, and the proposition in the main text is conditional on the audit passing.

